 "narrative": "Most of the new screen is null or clearly below the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold. feature_060, feature_033, feature_050, feature_046 level_003 versus level_001, feature_047, feature_017, feature_043, feature_022, and feature_064 all have point estimates far below threshold or intervals centered near zero; both signed directions can be rejected and closed. feature_016 is also below threshold despite an interval that crosses the boundary, so it is not accepted. The main exception is feature_027. H89 requested the positive raw direction and received signed estimate -0.792, interval -0.907 to -0.676, so that positive claim is rejected. The pre-registered opposite claim H105, direction -1, therefore supports a raw negative exposed-minus-comparator association: feature_027=1 versus 0 is associated with a lower outcome_001 value, meaning stronger composite dependency, by about 0.79 units, with interval far above the threshold. I accept H105 as a dataset-specific full-cohort marginal association, but keep it active and request independent validation because the exposed cell is relatively sparse (130 versus 1870), this was discovered in a broad screen, and it may be correlated with the accepted trio. I also registered conditional refinements for feature_027 among feature_037 absent, feature_002 absent, feature_010 absent, and all three absent to assess whether it appears independent of the accepted markers rather than a proxy. feature_063 is another borderline candidate: H82 contradicted the positive direction, while H83 supports the negative raw direction with signed estimate +0.227, interval +0.131 to +0.323. The point exceeds threshold but the lower bound does not, so I keep H83 unresolved and active rather than accepting it; conditional refinements against accepted-marker-absent strata can clarify whether it is confounded or attenuated. All accepted or deferred conclusions remain associations within this supplied dataset, not causal claims or externally generalizable claims.",
 "research_notes": "Iteration 6 appraise. New accepted candidate: H105 feature_027=1 vs 0, negative raw direction (lower outcome_001, stronger dependency), signed +0.792, interval +0.676 to +0.907. Accepted dataset-specific marginal association, active pending validation and confounding refinement. Validation requested for H105. H89 rejected. feature_063 remains borderline: H83 signed +0.227, lower +0.131, so unresolved active; not validated now because interval lower bound is below threshold. H82 rejected. Most other new binary/categorical screens rejected closed: feature_060, feature_033, feature_050, feature_046 level_003 vs level_001, feature_047, feature_017, feature_043, feature_022, feature_064, feature_016, and their opposite claims. Registered refinements: feature_027 conditional on feature_037 absent, feature_002 absent, feature_010 absent, and triple absent; feature_063 conditional on triple absent and feature_037 absent. Future analysis priority: feature_027 refinements and validation response, then feature_063 refinements if useful. If feature_027 validation remains strong, close as accepted unless conditioning suggests severe confounding; if validation weakens below threshold, downgrade or reject. If feature_063 conditional results are not threshold-level, close or defer. Still defer feature_003 family and low-value exact continuous comparisons. Validation budget after request: remaining independent requests should be reserved for replication, not repeated near-threshold discovery.",
